  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Two lines of regression"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Regression is the estimation of one variable from another using the average relationship between them. The line of Y on X is $y - \\bar{y} = b_{yx}(x - \\bar{x})$ with $b_{yx} = r\\sigma_y/\\sigma_x = Cov(x, y)/\\sigma_x^2$; it estimates Y from X. The line of X on Y is $x - \\bar{x} = b_{xy}(y - \\bar{y})$ with $b_{xy} = r\\sigma_x/\\sigma_y$. Both are fitted by least squares.",
    "kn": "ಒಂದು ಚರಾಂಶದಿಂದ ಇನ್ನೊಂದರ ಅಂದಾಜು ಪ್ರತಿಗಮನ. X ಮೇಲೆ Y ರೇಖೆ: y − ȳ = b_yx(x − x̄), b_yx = rσᵧ/σₓ. Y ಮೇಲೆ X ರೇಖೆ: x − x̄ = b_xy(y − ȳ), b_xy = rσₓ/σᵧ. ಎರಡನ್ನೂ ಕನಿಷ್ಠ ವರ್ಗಗಳ ವಿಧಾನದಿಂದ ಹೊಂದಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Y on X: estimate Y"
    },
    {
     "en": "X on Y: estimate X"
    },
    {
     "en": "Both pass through (x̄, ȳ)"
    }
   ],
   "formula": "y - \\bar{y} = r\\frac{\\sigma_y}{\\sigma_x}(x - \\bar{x}), \\qquad x - \\bar{x} = r\\frac{\\sigma_x}{\\sigma_y}(y - \\bar{y})",
   "narration": {
    "en": "Regression is the estimation of one variable from another using the average relationship between them. The line of Y on X is y - \\bar{y} = b_{yx}(x - \\bar{x}) with b_{yx} = r\\sigma_y/\\sigma_x = Cov(x, y)/\\sigma_x^2; it estimates Y from X. The line of X on Y is x - \\bar{x} = b_{xy}(y - \\bar{y}) with b_{xy} = r\\sigma_x/\\sigma_y. Both are fitted by least squares.",
    "kn": "ಒಂದು ಚರಾಂಶದಿಂದ ಇನ್ನೊಂದರ ಅಂದಾಜು ಪ್ರತಿಗಮನ. X ಮೇಲೆ Y ರೇಖೆ: y − ȳ = b_yx(x − x̄), b_yx = rσᵧ/σₓ. Y ಮೇಲೆ X ರೇಖೆ: x − x̄ = b_xy(y − ȳ), b_xy = rσₓ/σᵧ. ಎರಡನ್ನೂ ಕನಿಷ್ಠ ವರ್ಗಗಳ ವಿಧಾನದಿಂದ ಹೊಂದಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ."
   }
  },
